! Zone-based firewall (ZBFW) - stateful filtering between zones
!
! Replaces classic ACLs at the edge: traffic is allowed only when it
! matches a zone-pair policy, and the firewall tracks session state.
!
! Define zones matching the network-designs zoning model
zone security DMZ
zone security INTERNAL
zone security MGMT
zone security WAN

! Assign interfaces to zones
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 zone-member security WAN
!
interface GigabitEthernet0/1.10
 zone-member security DMZ
!
interface GigabitEthernet0/1.20
 zone-member security INTERNAL

! Classify traffic (e.g. web from WAN to DMZ)
class-map type inspect match-any DMZ-WEB
 match protocol http
 match protocol https
!
class-map type inspect match-any INTERNAL-DNS
 match protocol dns

! Policy: what is allowed WAN -> DMZ (nothing else)
policy-map type inspect WAN-TO-DMZ-POLICY
 class type inspect DMZ-WEB
  inspect
 class class-default
  drop

! Policy: allow full session state INTERNAL -> DMZ + WAN
policy-map type inspect INTERNAL-TO-OUT
 class class-default
  inspect

! Bind policies to zone pairs
zone-pair security WAN-DMZ source WAN destination DMZ
 service-policy type inspect WAN-TO-DMZ-POLICY
!
zone-pair security INTERNAL-DMZ source INTERNAL destination DMZ
 service-policy type inspect INTERNAL-TO-OUT
!
zone-pair security INTERNAL-WAN source INTERNAL destination WAN
 service-policy type inspect INTERNAL-TO-OUT

! Default zone-pair policy drops everything not explicitly matched

! Verify
! show policy-map type inspect zone-pair
! show zone security
! show zone-pair security
